Think: For each path in txt_file_list.txt, produce a line with relative path (relative to /home/student/files), size in bytes, and number of lines, and write those records to analysis_workspace/line_counts_raw.txt.

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
  path=$0;
  rel=path;
  sub("^/home/student/files/","",rel);
  cmd = "stat -c%s \"" path "\"";
  cmd | getline size;
  close(cmd);
  cmd2 = "wc -l < \"" path "\"";
  cmd2 | getline lines;
  close(cmd2);
  print rel " " size " " lines;
}' analysis_workspace/txt_file_list.txt > analysis_workspace/line_counts_raw.txt
